    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass, including the new `Cp50Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**The change:**\n- Added an in-memory idempotency store (`idempotencyKeyToOwnerId`, a `ConcurrentHashMap`) mapping each seen `Idempotency-Key` to the id of the owner originally created under it.\n- At the start of `addOwner`, if the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` that's already recorded, it looks up and returns the originally created owner with **200 OK** \u2014 skipping all the create/validation logic that would otherwise reject the repeat as a 409 duplicate.\n- After a successful `saveOwner`, it records the key \u2192 new owner id so a subsequent repeat is recognized.\n- Added a `currentIdempotencyKey()` helper that reads the `Idempotency-Key` header from the current request via `RequestContextHolder` \u2014 necessary because the `addOwner` signature comes from the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface (`interfaceOnly: true`) and has no header parameter, so I avoided coupling to the generator's parameter ordering.\n\n**Why this design:** The header lookup keeps the change localized to the controller without touching the generated API contract. Both create calls in a test run within the same test-managed transaction, so the second call's `findOwnerById` sees the first owner. Keys are unique per request, and the guard falls through to a normal create if a recorded id no longer resolves.\n\n**Verification:** `Cp50Tests` (the idempotency checkpoint) passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 62, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
