    "probe_text": "Reading the code as it stands, here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`. The request body is an **`OwnerFieldsDto`** (not the `Owner` entity), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Bean Validation on the DTO** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody` triggers JSR-380 constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/apostrophe/hyphen)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address`: `@Pattern(non-blank)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1`: `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`; `email`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `registrationDate` / `birthDate`: `@Valid` cascade\n   - A failure here \u2192 400 (and a DEBUG log in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Inside `addOwner`, in execution order\n\n3. **Idempotency lookup** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header; if the key was seen before, returns the previously-created owner as `200 OK` and short-circuits everything below (in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`).\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via MapStruct (`toOwner`), ignoring `id` and `pets`.\n5. **`applyAddress` / `normalizeAddress`** \u2014 requires `addressLine1` or flat `address`; trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST/RD/AVE`; sets `addressLine1/2` and composed `address`. \u2192 `InvalidAddressException` (400).\n6. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 supplied registration date after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n7. **Default registration date** to `LocalDate.now()` if null.\n8. **`toBusinessDay`** \u2014 rolls weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays forward; stores the adjusted date on the owner.\n9. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 counts existing owners with the same registration date; `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n10. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 `>= 50` owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n11. **`normalizeTelephone`** \u2014 strips formatting, assumes `+61`, enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length; stores E.164 value \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n12. **`normalizeEmail`** \u2014 optional; lower-cases; must match email pattern (`InvalidEmailException`, 400); rejects disposable domains mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail (`DisposableEmailException`, 400).\n13. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 optional; 4 digits; region-range check NSW/VIC/QLD \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400); stores validated postcode.\n14. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 rejects if a non-deleted owner shares normalized telephone + email \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n15. **`rejectDuplicateHousehold`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, rejects if a non-deleted owner shares the derived household id (last name + postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).\n16. **`assignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<sha256 hash8>`, de-duplicated with a `-n` suffix by scanning all owners.\n17. **`countNamesakes`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount`.\n18. **`computeBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when `> 80` owners share the registration day.\n19. **`countHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = matching members + 1.\n20. **`findPossibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 soft-duplicate detection (same last name + postcode, different phone, non-deleted, lowest id); sets `possibleDuplicateOf` and `possibleDuplicate` (skipped when `sharesHousehold`).\n21. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 `em.persist` (new id). At flush, Hibernate re-validates the **`Owner` entity** constraints: `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, and `telephone` `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (E.164).\n22. **Idempotency store write** \u2014 records `key \u2192 owner.getId()`.\n23. **AUDIT log** \u2014 dedicated `AUDIT` logger emits an INFO line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026 membershipNumber=\u2026`).\n24. **`Location` header** set to `/api/owners/{id}`; responds `201 CREATED` with the mapped `OwnerDto`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.), **no** `ApplicationEvent` publishing, and **no** password encoding anywhere in this path.\n- The outbound `OwnerDto` mapping computes many derived read-only fields (salutation, displayName, initials, Luhn check digit, membership number/level/points, locality, timezone, etc.), but these are response-shaping only \u2014 they are not persisted.\n\nThe core steps that actually mutate or reject are: **auth \u2192 DTO validation \u2192 address \u2192 registration-date rules \u2192 daily/city capacity \u2192 phone/email/postcode normalization \u2192 duplicate identity/household \u2192 derived-field enrichment \u2192 persist (+ entity-level validation) \u2192 idempotency record \u2192 audit log**."
